<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">spoilage</ansi>

Raw goods you cut from a carcass do not keep. Meat, fat, gut and organs go
off in a day or two of game time; raw hides and pelts in four or five. Rotten
goods are thrown out, and merchants pay less the closer something is to
turning. (A game day is about an hour of real time.)

Stop the clock by processing:

  <ansi fg="yellow">hides</ansi>    cure them with a hide scraper and salt at a tanning rack
  <ansi fg="yellow">furs</ansi>     make them into garments (the recipe cures them)
  <ansi fg="yellow">meat</ansi>     smoke it, dry it into jerky or cook it at a cooking fire
  <ansi fg="yellow">fat</ansi>      render it into tallow

Shop-bought goods never spoil, and goods kept in bank storage do not rot.

